<section class="api-class" id="sycl-property-queue-in-order">
<h3><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">sycl::property::queue::in_order</span></code><a class="headerlink" href="#sycl-property-queue-in-order" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h3>
<p>The <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">in_order</span></code> property adds the requirement that a <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">sycl::queue</span></code> provides
in-order semantics whereby commands submitted to said <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">sycl::queue</span></code> are
executed in the order in which they are submitted.
Commands submitted in this fashion can be viewed as-if having an implicit
dependence on the previous command submitted to that <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">sycl::queue</span></code>.
Using the <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">in_order</span></code> property makes no guarantees about the ordering
of commands submitted to different queues with respect to each other.</p>
